---
import LeadLayout from '../../layouts/LeadLayout.astro';
import { siteBase } from '../../lib/site';
import { breadcrumb } from '../../lib/schema';

const SITE = siteBase(Astro.site);
const path = '/zero-ban-protocol/checklist/';
const title = 'The Zero-Ban Protocol Checklist | AdBoost Health';
const description = 'The compliance protocol we run on every peptide and GLP-1 Meta account before we spend a dollar: lane, warm-up, copy, creative, escalation.';
const BOOK = '/book/?utm_source=lead-magnet&utm_medium=checklist&utm_campaign=zero-ban-protocol';
const PDF = '/downloads/zero-ban-protocol.pdf';
const jsonLd = [breadcrumb(SITE, [{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'The Zero-Ban Protocol', href: path }])];
---
<LeadLayout {title} {description} canonicalPath={path} {jsonLd} tag="The Zero-Ban Protocol">
  <section class="zbc">
    <div class="zbc-wrap">
      <header class="zbc-head">
        <span class="zbc-eyebrow">THE ZERO-BAN PROTOCOL</span>
        <h1>The compliance protocol behind $50K/month in peptide &amp; GLP-1 Meta ad spend, with <em>zero bans</em>.</h1>
        <p class="zbc-lede">Run this against your own account before your next launch. It&rsquo;s the exact protocol we run on every peptide and GLP-1 account before we spend a dollar. Work top to bottom, and don&rsquo;t skip the foundation.</p>
        <div class="zbc-meta">
          <span class="zbc-tagm">5 checkpoints</span>
          <span class="zbc-tagm">Run before launch</span>
          <span class="zbc-tagm">Peptide · GLP-1</span>
          <a class="zbc-pdf" href={PDF} download>
            <svg width="14" height="14" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3v12m0 0l-4-4m4 4l4-4M4 19h16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            Download PDF
          </a>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="zbc-frame">
        <span class="zbc-frame-label">Why bans happen</span>
        <p>Bans aren&rsquo;t random. Meta is a social platform, and its whole job is keeping people on it and feeling good while they&rsquo;re there. Every rejection you&rsquo;ll ever get traces back to something that threatened that experience. Get that frame and the rest of this protocol makes sense.</p>
      </div>

      <ol class="zbc-steps">
        <li class="zbc-cp" id="lane">
          <div class="zbc-rail"><span class="zbc-code">00</span></div>
          <div class="zbc-body">
            <span class="zbc-cp-tag">Foundation</span>
            <h2>Know your lane</h2>
            <p>Two completely different compliance lanes exist, and brands constantly run one while set up like the other. Figure out your lane before you build anything. Everything below assumes you got this right.</p>
            <ul class="zbc-do">
              <li><strong>Lane A: research-use-only peptides.</strong> No prescription involved, no LegitScript certification required.</li>
              <li><strong>Lane B: prescription / telehealth.</strong> GLP-1, ED, hair loss, anything dispensed against a script. <a href="/glossary/legitscript-certification/">LegitScript certification</a> is required by Meta, full stop; it doesn&rsquo;t verify you itself, it defers to the certifier.</li>
              <li>Confirm you are <strong>not in the dangerous middle</strong>: advertising pure peptides for human use with no legitimate prescription pathway, the highest-risk lane, where most catastrophic bans happen.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li class="zbc-cp" id="warm">
          <div class="zbc-rail"><span class="zbc-code">01</span></div>
          <div class="zbc-body">
            <span class="zbc-cp-tag">Setup</span>
            <h2>Warm the account before you sell it anything</h2>
            <p>Do not launch a cold account, a new card, or a fresh business manager straight into a conversion campaign. You&rsquo;re not buying results in week one. You&rsquo;re buying a clean record.</p>
            <ul class="zbc-do">
              <li>Run a <strong>preliminary awareness campaign for 3&ndash;7 days</strong> at a low daily budget.</li>
              <li>Confirm the <strong>card processes</strong> and the account can spend. Billing gets funky on new accounts in this vertical, so discover it on a low-budget test, not a scale push.</li>
              <li>Get <strong>ad approvals on record</strong>: a clean history, baseline data, and rapport with the platform before you ask it for anything expensive.</li>
              <li>Only graduate to a conversion campaign once you see <strong>clean approvals, no rejections, no payment flags</strong>.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="zbc-sticky">&ldquo;You&rsquo;re not buying results in week one. You&rsquo;re buying a clean record.&rdquo;</p>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li class="zbc-cp" id="copy">
          <div class="zbc-rail"><span class="zbc-code">02</span></div>
          <div class="zbc-body">
            <span class="zbc-cp-tag">Copy</span>
            <h2>Write copy that doesn&rsquo;t trip review</h2>
            <p>The headline and primary text are the most-scanned surface on your ad. Treat them as the most conservative part of the whole campaign.</p>
            <ul class="zbc-dont">
              <li>No scientific or clinical terminology in headlines and primary text.</li>
              <li>Don&rsquo;t name the compound. Early on, avoid the word &ldquo;peptide&rdquo; in captions entirely.</li>
              <li>Don&rsquo;t imply human usage or promise physiological outcomes; the line most people cross without realising it.</li>
              <li>No harsh claims and nothing that makes the reader feel bad about themselves. Shaming ads threaten the user experience, so Meta kills them.</li>
            </ul>
            <p><strong>The escalation principle:</strong> conservative copy on a cold account isn&rsquo;t timid. It&rsquo;s how you buy permission to be aggressive later. Lead with brand-level, lifestyle, benefit-adjacent language.</p>

            <div class="zbc-teardown" data-reveal>
              <div class="zbc-td-col rejected">
                <span class="zbc-td-tag">&#10005; REJECTED</span>
                <p class="zbc-td-ad">&ldquo;Our clinical-grade semaglutide peptide helps you lose up to 20 lbs in your first month, no diet, no gym.&rdquo;</p>
                <p class="zbc-td-why"><strong>Why it died:</strong> names the compound, leans on clinical terminology, and promises a physiological outcome with a number: three review triggers stacked into one line, on an account with no history to defend it.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="zbc-td-col compliant">
                <span class="zbc-td-tag">&#10003; COMPLIANT</span>
                <p class="zbc-td-ad">&ldquo;Ready to feel like yourself again? Here&rsquo;s the approach our clients are using to get there, without the guesswork.&rdquo;</p>
                <p class="zbc-td-why"><strong>Why it runs:</strong> benefit-adjacent, no compound named, no outcome promised, nothing that shames the reader. It sells the shift, not the substance.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li class="zbc-cp" id="creative">
          <div class="zbc-rail"><span class="zbc-code">03</span></div>
          <div class="zbc-body">
            <span class="zbc-cp-tag">Creative</span>
            <h2>Creative that passes review</h2>
            <p>The review system looks at your creative just as hard as your copy, and this is where health brands get banned fastest.</p>
            <ul class="zbc-dont">
              <li><strong>No before-and-after images. Ever.</strong> The imagery is often near-explicit and makes viewers feel bad about their bodies.</li>
              <li><strong>GLP-1 specifically: no brand names on product images or vials.</strong> Unbranded product only.</li>
            </ul>
            <ul class="zbc-do">
              <li><strong>Sell the transformation without showing a transformation.</strong> Show the change with objects, props, and symbolic before-and-afters: nothing about the human body, everything about the idea of change.</li>
              <li>Same escalation principle as copy: <strong>conservative creative first, aggressive later</strong>, once the account has approvals behind it.</li>
            </ul>

            <div class="zbc-teardown" data-reveal>
              <div class="zbc-td-col rejected">
                <span class="zbc-td-tag">&#10005; REJECTED</span>
                <p class="zbc-td-ad">Split-screen before-and-after of a woman&rsquo;s midsection, with a vial labelled &ldquo;Semaglutide&rdquo; in the corner.</p>
                <p class="zbc-td-why"><strong>Why it died:</strong> before-and-after body imagery is the single fastest ban in this vertical, and the branded compound on the vial is a second trigger on the same asset.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="zbc-td-col compliant">
                <span class="zbc-td-tag">&#10003; COMPLIANT</span>
                <p class="zbc-td-ad">One clean lifestyle frame: a pair of jeans that finally button, or an unbranded pen-style applicator on a bright kitchen counter.</p>
                <p class="zbc-td-why"><strong>Why it runs:</strong> the transformation is implied through objects, not bodies, and the product is unbranded. It passes review and still sells the outcome.</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </li>

        <li class="zbc-cp" id="escalate">
          <div class="zbc-rail"><span class="zbc-code">04</span></div>
          <div class="zbc-body">
            <span class="zbc-cp-tag">Scale</span>
            <h2>Earn the right to run aggressive</h2>
            <p>Everything up to now has been buying permission. This is spending it, but carefully.</p>
            <ul class="zbc-do">
              <li>Only once the account has <strong>consistent approvals and real spend history</strong>, start testing the aggressive angles that actually convert.</li>
              <li><strong>Test aggressive angles one at a time.</strong> Push five at once and something gets flagged. You&rsquo;ve learned nothing and spent your account&rsquo;s credibility.</li>
              <li>The real asset is <strong>account history, not your creative library.</strong> Every clean approval makes the next aggressive test survivable. A ban doesn&rsquo;t restart you at zero. It restarts you below zero.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div class="zbc-recap" data-reveal>
        <span class="zbc-recap-label">The 6 triggers that kill health ads fastest</span>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Before-and-after imagery.</strong> The single fastest ban. <span>Creative</span></li>
          <li><strong>Naming the compound</strong>: &ldquo;peptide,&rdquo; &ldquo;semaglutide,&rdquo; or a brand on a vial. <span>Copy &middot; Creative</span></li>
          <li><strong>Promising a physiological outcome</strong>: &ldquo;lose X lbs,&rdquo; &ldquo;boost testosterone.&rdquo; <span>Copy</span></li>
          <li><strong>Clinical or scientific terminology</strong> in headlines and primary text. <span>Copy</span></li>
          <li><strong>Shaming or insecurity-baiting</strong>: anything that makes the reader feel bad. <span>Copy &middot; Creative</span></li>
          <li><strong>Going aggressive on a cold account</strong> with no history to spend. <span>Warm-up &middot; Scale</span></li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <div class="zbc-cta gcard">
        <div>
          <span class="zbc-cta-status">● CLEARED FOR LAUNCH</span>
          <h3>Want us to just run this for you?</h3>
          <p>We manage peptide and GLP-1 accounts spending $10K/month and up: compliance, creative, attribution, and scale. Book a free strategy call and we&rsquo;ll pressure-test your account against this exact protocol.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="zbc-cta-btn" href={BOOK}>Book a strategy call &rarr;</a>
      </div>

      <p class="zbc-disclaimer">This is practitioner guidance based on how we run health-vertical ad accounts, not legal advice. Platform policies change; verify against Meta&rsquo;s current advertising standards and your own compliance counsel before launch.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style>
    /* the page's own names, mapped onto the system's roles so it reads in both schemes and prints clean */
    .zbc {
      --z-blue: var(--accent); --z-ink: var(--fg); --z-ink2: var(--fg-2); --z-mute: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 62%, transparent);
      --z-line: var(--line); --z-do: var(--st-ok); --z-dont: var(--st-warn); --z-surface: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 4%, var(--bg));
      padding: clamp(40px, 6vw, 72px) 0 10px;
    }
    .zbc-wrap { max-width: calc(760px + 2 * var(--pad)); margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 var(--pad); }

    .zbc-head { padding: 0 0 28px; }
    .zbc-eyebrow { font: 500 12.5px/1.3 var(--sans); letter-spacing: .22em; color: var(--z-ink2); }
    .zbc-eyebrow::before { content: ""; display: inline-block; width: 6px; height: 6px; margin-right: 8px; vertical-align: .1em; background: var(--z-blue); }
    .zbc-head h1 { font-size: clamp(34px, 4.6vw, 56px); line-height: 1.08; letter-spacing: -.022em; margin: 16px 0 18px; text-wrap: balance; }
    .zbc-head h1 em { font-style: italic; }
    .zbc-lede { font-size: clamp(17px, 1.3vw, 19px); line-height: 1.62; color: var(--z-ink2); margin: 0 0 24px; }
    .zbc-meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 10px; }
    .zbc-tagm { font-size: 14px; color: var(--z-ink2); border-radius: 999px; padding: 6px 13px; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--z-line); }
    .zbc-pdf { margin-left: auto; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; min-height: 44px; font-size: 15px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--z-ink); border-radius: 999px; padding: 0 18px; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--z-ink); transition: box-shadow .3s var(--spring-snap); }
    .zbc-pdf:hover { box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--z-ink), 0 0 0 5px color-mix(in srgb, var(--z-blue) 14%, transparent); }

    .zbc-frame { border-left: 2px solid var(--z-blue); padding: 4px 0 4px 22px; margin: 6px 0 12px; }
    .zbc-frame-label { display: block; font: 500 12.5px/1.3 var(--sans); letter-spacing: .22em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--z-ink2); margin-bottom: 10px; }
    .zbc-frame p { margin: 0; font: 300 clamp(19px, 1.6vw, 23px) / 1.4 var(--serif); color: var(--z-ink); }

    /* the protocol's spine */
    .zbc-steps { margin: 0; padding: 0; }
    .zbc-cp { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 56px 1fr; gap: 20px; padding: 32px 0; }
    .zbc-cp + .zbc-cp { border-top: 1px solid var(--z-line); }
    .zbc-rail { position: relative; }
    .zbc-code { position: sticky; top: 26px; display: grid; place-items: center; width: 46px; height: 46px; border-radius: 50%; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--z-blue); color: var(--z-ink); font: 500 13px/1 var(--sans); letter-spacing: .06em; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
    .zbc-cp-tag { font: 500 12.5px/1.3 var(--sans); letter-spacing: .22em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--z-ink2); }
    .zbc-body h2 { font-size: clamp(26px, 2.4vw, 34px); line-height: 1.15; margin: 8px 0 12px; }
    .zbc-body > p { font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.62; color: var(--z-ink2); margin: 0 0 14px; }
    .zbc-body > p strong { color: var(--z-ink); font-weight: 500; }
    .zbc-body a { color: var(--z-ink); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: var(--z-blue); text-underline-offset: 3px; }
    .zbc-sticky { font: italic 300 21px/1.4 var(--serif) !important; color: var(--z-ink) !important; margin: 16px 0 0 !important; }

    /* do and don't: a tick or a cross in a tinted square, drawn in CSS so they follow the scheme */
    .zbc-do, .zbc-dont { margin: 0 0 8px; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: 11px; }
    .zbc-do li, .zbc-dont li { position: relative; padding-left: 32px; font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.56; color: var(--z-ink2); }
    .zbc-do li strong, .zbc-dont li strong { color: var(--z-ink); font-weight: 500; }
    .zbc-do li::before, .zbc-dont li::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 3px; width: 20px; height: 20px; border-radius: 6px; }
    .zbc-do li::before { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--z-do) 14%, transparent); }
    .zbc-do li::after { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 6px; top: 8px; width: 8px; height: 5px; border-left: 2px solid var(--z-do); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--z-do); rotate: -45deg; }
    .zbc-dont { margin-top: 4px; }
    .zbc-dont li::before {
      background:
        linear-gradient(45deg, transparent calc(50% - 1px), var(--z-dont) calc(50% - 1px) calc(50% + 1px), transparent calc(50% + 1px)) center / 9px 9px no-repeat,
        linear-gradient(-45deg, transparent calc(50% - 1px), var(--z-dont) calc(50% - 1px) calc(50% + 1px), transparent calc(50% + 1px)) center / 9px 9px no-repeat,
        color-mix(in srgb, var(--z-dont) 13%, transparent);
    }

    /* worked teardown: rejected, then compliant */
    .zbc-teardown { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 12px; margin: 20px 0 4px; }
    .zbc-td-col { border-radius: var(--r-media); padding: 18px 18px 16px; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--z-line); }
    .zbc-td-col.rejected { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--z-dont) 6%, transparent); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--z-dont) 26%, transparent); }
    .zbc-td-col.compliant { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--z-do) 6%, transparent); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--z-do) 28%, transparent); }
    .zbc-td-tag { display: inline-block; font: 500 12.5px/1.3 var(--sans); letter-spacing: .16em; margin-bottom: 12px; }
    .zbc-td-col.rejected .zbc-td-tag { color: var(--z-dont); }
    .zbc-td-col.compliant .zbc-td-tag { color: var(--z-do); }
    .zbc-td-ad { font: italic 300 18px/1.45 var(--serif); color: var(--z-ink); margin: 0 0 10px; }
    .zbc-td-why { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--z-ink2); margin: 0; }
    .zbc-td-why strong { color: var(--z-ink); font-weight: 500; }

    /* the trigger recap */
    .zbc-recap { border-radius: var(--r-panel); padding: clamp(20px, 2.4vw, 30px); margin: 32px 0 12px; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--z-line); }
    .zbc-recap-label { display: block; font: 500 12.5px/1.3 var(--sans); letter-spacing: .22em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--z-ink2); margin-bottom: 16px; }
    .zbc-recap ol { margin: 0; padding-left: 22px; display: grid; gap: 10px; list-style: decimal; }
    .zbc-recap li { font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.5; color: var(--z-ink2); }
    .zbc-recap li::marker { color: var(--z-blue); }
    .zbc-recap li strong { color: var(--z-ink); font-weight: 500; }
    .zbc-recap li span { color: var(--z-mute); font-size: 14px; }

    /* the closing call to action: a gradient card */
    .zbc-cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 22px; justify-content: space-between; margin: 34px 0 20px; }
    .zbc-cta-status { font: 500 12.5px/1.3 var(--sans); letter-spacing: .16em; color: var(--st-ok); }
    .zbc-cta h3 { font-size: clamp(24px, 2.2vw, 30px); margin: 10px 0 8px; }
    .zbc-cta p { font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--fg-2); margin: 0; max-width: 46ch; }
    .zbc-cta-btn { flex: none; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 52px; padding: 0 26px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--accent-color); color: var(--accent-fg); font-weight: 500; font-size: 15px; white-space: nowrap; box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-frame) 14%, transparent); transition: box-shadow .4s var(--spring-snap); }
    .zbc-cta-btn:hover { box-shadow: 0 0 0 6px color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent-frame) 18%, transparent); }
    .zbc-disclaimer { font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--z-mute); margin: 0 0 10px; }

    @media (max-width: 560px) {
      .zbc-cp { grid-template-columns: 38px 1fr; gap: 14px; }
      .zbc-code { width: 36px; height: 36px; font-size: 12.5px; top: 20px; }
      .zbc-cta { flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; }
      .zbc-cta-btn { width: 100%; justify-content: center; }
      .zbc-teardown { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .zbc-pdf { margin-left: 0; }
    }

    /* clean print / PDF: the light scheme's roles on white, whatever the reader's scheme, everything
       arrived, nothing interactive */
    @media print {
      .zbc {
        --fg: var(--frame); --fg-2: color-mix(in srgb, var(--frame) 80%, transparent); --bg: transparent;
        --line: color-mix(in srgb, var(--frame) 18%, transparent); --accent: var(--accent-paper);
        --st-ok: var(--ok); --st-warn: var(--warn); color: var(--frame); padding: 0;
      }
      .zbc-pdf, .zbc-cta-btn { display: none !important; }
      .zbc-wrap { max-width: none; padding: 0; }
      .zbc-code { position: static; }
      .zbc-cp, .zbc-teardown, .zbc-recap, .zbc-cta { break-inside: avoid; page-break-inside: avoid; }
      [data-reveal] { opacity: 1 !important; transform: none !important; }
      .zbc-td-col, .zbc-recap, .zbc-do li::before, .zbc-dont li::before { -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact; print-color-adjust: exact; }
      .zbc-cta { background: none; box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--line); color: var(--frame); --fg: var(--frame); --fg-2: color-mix(in srgb, var(--frame) 80%, transparent); }
      .zbc-cta-status { color: var(--ok); }
      a { color: var(--accent-paper) !important; text-decoration: none; }
    }
  </style>
</LeadLayout>
